# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# asdf version management
.tool-versions

node_modules
.cursorignore
.turbo

.env*
!*.env.example

# cursor
bun.lockb

# content-collections
.content-collections

# Twiggy
.cursor/

.open-next

target/

.cargo-tools/

rust-migration-notes.md

# rasen machine-local store pointer. The rasen planning artifacts themselves
# (proposal, design, tasks, specs) are NOT in this worktree: the rasen project
# root for this repository is registered at the main checkout, whose working tree
# stays pinned and clean, so they live there as untracked local state. What this
# branch carries is the code plus the provenance documents — UPSTREAM.md,
# PATCHES.md, SBOM.md, SOURCE_INVENTORY.*, BOUNDARIES.md.
.rasen-store/

# wasm-pack output (rebuild correspondence check writes here)
rust/wasm/pkg/

# Vite example production build output. Untracked and unignored it is ~34 MB of
# generated files (271 copied flag SVGs and a 21.6 MB wasm among them), which
# would otherwise land in a commit.
apps/vite-example/dist/
# C4 fresh-build evidence uses exclusive output directories so an earlier
# production artifact can never be mistaken for the build under test.
apps/vite-example/dist-c4-*/
apps/web/.next-c4-*/
# Electron host production build output, the same class of artefact as the
# vite-example dist above: ~34 MB of generated files (the copied runtime-asset
# allowlist and the wasm among them) regenerated by every
# `bun run --cwd apps/electron-host build`.
apps/electron-host/dist/
# The main-process store seam compiled to CJS by the same build script
# (`bun build … --outfile=dist-main/main-store-ipc.cjs`) — a small generated
# bundle, kept out of commits for the same reason as the renderer dist.
apps/electron-host/dist-main/
# Emitted distributable Surface stylesheet, built by
# `apps/vite-example/vite.surface-css.config.ts`. `check-surface-css-boundary.mjs`
# reads it straight off disk rather than out of git, so ignoring it costs the
# check nothing and keeps a ~119 kB generated sheet out of commits. The
# unanchored pattern also covers a stray root-level `dist-surface-css/` if the
# config is ever run from the wrong working directory.
dist-surface-css/

# SDK tarball packing output (`script/pack-sdk-tarballs.mjs`, S05 P3). The
# tarballs are machine-local build artifacts; the committed evidence is the
# digest manifest written into the change's evidence directory, never the
# tarballs themselves.
dist-sdk-tarballs/

# Distributable runtime bundle output (`script/pack-runtime.mjs`, S08 R group 4).
# Same class as the tarball dir above: machine-local build artifacts, the
# committed record is the evidence manifest written into the change's evidence
# directory.
dist-runtime/

# Parity-run output: screenshots, per-host snapshots and ledgers, plus
# Playwright's own scratch directories. Regenerated by `bun run test:parity`; the
# committed outcome is PARITY.md and the archived copies under the change's
# evidence directory. `.playwright/` is an earlier output location for the same
# run; a snapshot left there is named exactly like the real one and is a valid
# input to the documented diff command, so it is ignored rather than left
# committable.
apps/vite-example/tests/parity-artifacts/
apps/vite-example/tests/.pw-output/
apps/vite-example/tests/.playwright/

# Migration- and stickers-probe output, the same class of artefact as above but
# from `playwright.probe.config.ts` rather than the parity run. Left uncovered
# these were ~18 committable PNG/JSON files, and `probe-<host>.json` carries a
# verbatim copy of a persisted project record — the exact shape of leak the
# `.playwright/` rule above exists to prevent.
apps/vite-example/tests/probe-artifacts/
apps/vite-example/tests/.pw-output-probe/

# C3 backend-specific session harness output. The test and config are source;
# traces, reports and any persisted browser profile remain machine-local.
apps/vite-example/tests/c3-artifacts/
apps/vite-example/tests/.pw-output-c3/
apps/vite-example/tests/.pw-output-c5-storage/
